          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is Ontario Education Online Ministry inspected?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. Ontario Education Online (BSID: 882902) is inspected by the Ontario Ministry of Education and authorized to grant Ontario Secondary School Diploma (OSSD) credits for Grades 9–12.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_gfeAw9": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will OEO credits appear on an official transcript?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. Credits are recorded on an official transcript. </p><p>For part-time students, we send the credit to the school maintaining the OSR.</p><p>For full-time students, OEO maintains the OSR and issues transcripts directly.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_Pincxi": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can students apply to OUAC using OEO marks?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. Students can use their OEO marks when applying to Ontario universities through OUAC.</p><p>Students must list <strong>Ontario Education Online (OEO)</strong> as one of their schools on their OUAC application. Once listed, our administrative team can upload midterm and/or final marks directly to OUAC.</p><p>Students are responsible for notifying us once they have applied and added OEO to their application so we can ensure marks are uploaded before university deadlines.</p><p>If you are unsure about timelines, we are happy to guide you through the process.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_7dNLT9": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are courses live or self-paced?",
            "content": "<p>All courses are fully asynchronous. Students work at their own pace within the allowed timeframe.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_BffVUG": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long does a course take to complete",
            "content": "<p>Students can complete a course in as little as <strong>4 weeks</strong>, or they have up to <strong>12 months from their start date</strong> to finish.</p><p>Because OEO is fully asynchronous, students move at their own pace. Motivated students often accelerate, while others choose a slower schedule to balance athletics, work, or other commitments. All courses are designed to meet the Ontario Ministry requirement of <strong>110 instructional hours per credit</strong>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_8Dc4zf": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How is each course designed?",
            "content": "<p>Each course is designed for 110 hours of learning:</p><p>• 50 lessons (approximately 2 hours each)</p><p>• 10-hour Culminating Performance Task (CPT)</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_yhetRf": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are teachers Ontario Certified Teachers (OCT)?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. All courses are taught and assessed by Ontario Certified Teachers.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_EzEMXb": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are there final exams?",
            "content": "<p>No. OEO does not require final exams. Instead, each course includes a 30% Culminating Performance Task (CPT).</p><p>We believe this provides a more meaningful demonstration of student learning and eliminates the need for exam proctors.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_FBDePD": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How quickly are assignments marked?",
            "content": "<p>• Teachers respond to messages within 24 hours (Mon-Fri)</p><p>• Assessments are marked and returned within 48–72 hours (Mon-Fri)</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_89HfDw": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do you offer cooperative education (co-op)?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. OEO specializes in cooperative education placements across Ontario (and abroad), including in-person placements supported by structured online pre-placement modules. This is a rare offering among online private schools.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_ecdQgP": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How is co-op structured?",
            "content": "<p>Each co-op credit (110 hours) includes:</p><p>• 10 structured online pre-placement modules (resume writing, interview preparation, workplace safety training, professionalism, goal setting)</p><p>• Approximately 100 hours of in-person placement with an approved employer per credit</p><p>• Ongoing OCT teacher supervision</p><p>• Midterm and final evaluations completed with the workplace supervisor</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_dy3w7p": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can co-op hours count toward apprenticeship?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. For eligible skilled trades placements, OEO can generate a Registered Training Agreement (RTA) so co-op hours may count toward an apprenticeship pathway.</p><p>Very few online OR private schools offer this level of skilled trades support.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_DYQnDk": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are there hidden fees?",
            "content": "<p>No.</p><p>Tuition includes course access, teacher support, marking, and transcript issuance. There are no hidden textbook or platform fees.<br/><br/>In certain situations, additional administrative fees may apply, such as:</p><p>• PLAR (Prior Learning Assessment and Recognition) reviews</p><p>• International transcript evaluation or credit assessment</p><p>• Specialized documentation requests</p><p>Any such fees are discussed transparently with families before proceeding.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_pRdWzY": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is your refund policy?",
            "content": "<p>We strongly encourage families to reach out before registering to ensure the course is the right fit—our team is always happy to help guide your decision.</p><p>Once a course has been purchased and access has been granted, refunds are not provided due to immediate access to course materials and teacher allocation.</p><p>If you have any questions before enrolling, we highly recommend booking a guidance session so we can support you in making the best choice.</p>"
          }
        }
